---
title: Choreography
layout: layouts/base.njk
eleventyNavigation:
  key: Choreography
  order: 2
---

<div class="choreography-page">
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="intro">
  I dabble in contra choreography.
  Most dances I write its because there is a hook or move that I want to
  call, but I could not find a dance that meets that audience's needs.
  </p>


  <div class="dance-list">
    {% for dance in choreography %}
      <article class="dance-card">
        <h2 class="dance-title">
          <a href="/choreography/{{ dance.slug }}/">
            {{ dance.title }}
          </a>
        </h2>
        <div class="dance-meta">
          <span class="dance-formation">{{ dance.formation }}</span>
          {% if dance.progression %}
            <span class="meta-divider">·</span>
            <span class="dance-progression">{{ dance.progression }}</span>
          {% endif %}
          {% if dance.author %}
            <span class="meta-divider">·</span>
            <span class="dance-author">by {{ dance.author }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% if dance.notes and dance.notes.length > 0 %}
          <p class="dance-preview">{{ dance.notes[0] | truncate(120) }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="intro">
  Consider any of these dances as in the public domain.
  Dances in our tradition don't exist without the communities
  that dance them, I believe contra choreography belongs to the whole community.
  Someday I'll write a blog post to share more thoughts on the topic.
</p>
</div>